+
+### Large allocations: total free bytes are not the fit test
+
+On JDK 25.0.3, an object larger than one region needs a consecutive run of eligible regions
+in the mutator free set. Compare the failed allocation's **aligned object size**, including
+headers, with region size and the required region count. A 16 MiB object needs four 4 MiB
+regions; 24 MiB free in scattered regions need not satisfy it. This is a different constraint
+from finishing the concurrent cycle before aggregate headroom runs out.
+
+`-Xlog:gc+free=info` reports `Free:` for the mutator free set, `Max: … regular` for its
+largest per-region allocation capacity, and `… humongous` for its longest run of currently
+empty regions. Collector reserves appear separately; do not add them to a mutator request's
+contiguous budget. Match this snapshot to the failure time, GC phase and allocation size.
+It is not a reservation or a complete allocation oracle: intervening allocations change
+the run, and the allocation path can also recycle trash regions when concurrent weak-root
+processing permits, whereas the logged humongous maximum counts empty regions only.
+
+Missing failure-time evidence leaves fragmentation as a hypothesis. A fitting eligible run
+at the relevant instant defeats the simple "not enough contiguous regions" explanation;
+inspect the actual failure path before adjusting trigger thresholds. Do not select earlier
+marking or more GC workers solely from tail waste; check whether reclamation can create the
+needed run. Consider allocation shape, reclaimable regions and measured recovery; any change to object chunking, heap or
+region size must preserve behavior and be compared for footprint, waste and latency.
+
+Implementation evidence: [25.0.3 region-size predicate](https://github.com/openjdk/jdk25u/blob/jdk-25.0.3%2B9/src/hotspot/share/gc/shenandoah/shenandoahHeapRegion.hpp)
+(`requires_humongous`) and [25.0.3 free-set allocation and logging](https://github.com/openjdk/jdk25u/blob/jdk-25.0.3%2B9/src/hotspot/share/gc/shenandoah/shenandoahFreeSet.cpp)
+(`allocate_contiguous`, `can_allocate_from`, `log_status`). Recheck these details for another
+build; a percentage of `humongous waste` alone does not select a remedy.
 
